Z||000000||LAMBO||02-27-2001||05:41 PM||||This is a nonFiero-related problem I'm having with a 2.9l Bronco II. I'm desperate, so I'm posting here in hopes of someone being able to help me out. Just had a valve job on her and got it back together. She runs great, but very rich and quickly fouls plugs, then doesn't run so well. It doesn't seem to matter if it's at idle or WOT. Doesn't throw any codes from the computer to let me know what's up. What could it possibly be. Bad O2 sensor, other? Please help. I'm not having much luck figuring this one out. Again, sorry for posting non-fiero stuff here.<BR>Todd||||reg||5
Z||000001||strdream||02-27-2001||07:33 PM||||First I would check the MAP sensor.  Make sure it has good manifold vacuum to it. The vac lines may be crossed or something.<BR>Next check the (I think Ford calls it ACT).<BR>Air charge temp sensor.  A two wire sensor in the air passage of the intake manifold.<BR>Ross||||reg||1
Z||000002||hugh||02-27-2001||08:04 PM||||How did it run before the valve job?Did it foul plugs then?Have you checked the plug wires to know they are on the right plugs?Does it smoke?if so,when? What color is the smoke and how much is there?||||reg||1
Z||000003||LAMBO||02-27-2001||08:49 PM||||With clean plugs, it starts and runs fine. But you can immediately start to smell that rich burn and your eyes let you know too. Don't notice any smoke.<P>The reason it got a valve job was because of no compression in one hole (burnt valve, truck has 150k on it). Wasn't running real good at all, but it wasn't running rich like it is now. Maybe I'll try replacing the ACT first. Anything that controls the air/fuel mix could be the problem. Seems logical anyway. I just hate plunking down money on non-returnable parts, especially if they don't fix the problem. Any more insights would be greatly appreciated.<BR>Todd||||reg||1
Z||000004||hugh||02-27-2001||09:19 PM||||Todd,Is it always the same plugs?If so you may have reversed 2 wires that are close enough in the firing order to run ok but cause your problem(not likely but possible).The only thing I can suggest is to start from scratch and recheck every one of your steps.You may find a simple solution.unplugged sensor,air cleaner element,etc.I can think of nothing else to suggest.Good luck!  ||||reg||1
